WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
Split a uranium nucleus,
and energy is released.

2
00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.240
That is fission.

3
00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:06.750
Now do the opposite.

4
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.470
Join a hydrogen-2 nucleus
to a hydrogen-3 nucleus,

5
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.930
making helium and a spare neutron.

6
00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:19.070
That also releases energy:
17.6 MeV from one reaction.

7
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:27.490
Per nucleon, it beats fission: 3.5 MeV,
against about 0.85 for uranium fission.

8
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.540
Joining releases energy.

9
00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:31.810
Splitting releases energy.

10
00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.690
How can both be true?

11
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:37.530
In this mission, you'll put
fusion and fission side by side,

12
00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:40.330
and track what happens
to the nuclei in each.

13
00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:43.710
Then you'll decide which nuclear
reactions give out energy,

14
00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:45.870
and which need energy put in.

15
00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:50.680
Your mission: explain how joining and
splitting can both release energy.
